    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Iglesia de Piedra, a limestone Methodist church, earned a spot on the U.S. National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camuy%2C_Puerto_Rico"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1846 Puente Camuy bridge over the Camuy River linked the town with Hatillo, pioneering early regional connectivity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camuy%2C_Puerto_Rico"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Camuy belongs to Puerto Rico’s Porta Atlántico tourist area, underscoring its coastal heritage and maritime roots.",
